        "result": "I fixed the one finding, the `QUALITY_HIGH_CCN` on `UserController.apply` (cyclomatic complexity 13 against a threshold of 10). I haven't compiled or tested anything, since the orchestrator owns validation.\n\n**Change:** I split `apply` into smaller private methods in `user-service/src/main/java/com/juanesteban/tcc/user/UserController.java`:\n- `validate(ApplyRequest)` holds the null and positive-shares checks.\n- `applyBuy(...)` and `applySell(...)` hold the buy and sell logic.\n- `apply` now only validates the request, loads the user with the lock, and picks the buy or sell path.\n\nI expect the complexity of `apply` to drop below 10, but that needs the A2 re-run to confirm.\n\nThe order of checks and the status codes and messages are unchanged: 400 for an invalid request, 404 for an unknown user, 400 for an invalid type, insufficient funds or insufficient position. The transaction boundary and the flush before returning the state are unchanged. The public API, the architecture, the service topology and the databases are untouched.\n\n**One small difference:** the new `Position` in `applyBuy` takes its user id from `u.getId()` instead of the path `id`. They are the same value, because the user was loaded by that id.\n\nNothing is left unresolved.",
